      "content": "i mean, you say \"consensus\" but it feels like a lot of the actual planning research and \"modern\" experts are saying that single-family zoning is just a way to keep people out and drive up prices. is there even a real scientific argument for keeping it that way, or is it more just about protecting property values for people who already have homes?",
