      "content": "Researchers have indeed found that single-family zoning and suburbanization can have regressive effects, disproportionately affecting low-income and minority communities. Studies have shown that single-family zoning can limit diversity of land use, leading to segregation, pollution, and reduced community amenities. While property value protection is a concern, the scientific argument for single-family zoning largely revolves around it, rather than long-term benefits to society. Many experts argue that modern, inclusive, and sustainable urban planning should prioritize urban density, affordability, and community equity over preservation of property values.",
